"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[83484],{83484:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n<center>\\n<RestaurantCard\\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/location/2345f9eae1ea25b21988cd31114222eb.jpg\\"\\n          title=\\"Gongmuljip\\"\\n          cuisine=\\"Cafe\\"\\n          address=\\"12-1, Hyosim 1-gil, Gongju-si, Chungcheongnam-do\\"\\n          rating=3.0\\n          tags=\\"cafe\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Ordered\\n```menu\\n{\\n\\"title\\": \\"Misu Sampler\\",\\n\\"rating\\": 4\\n}\\n---\\nIt was fascinating how the flavors varied depending on the type of bean, and the Seonbijabi bean, with its sweet and rich flavor, was the most delicious.\\n```\\n```menu\\n{\\n\\"title\\": \\"Signature Drip Coffee\\",\\n\\"rating\\": 3.5\\n}\\n---\\nWhile I couldn\'t strongly detect the grain presence, it was a nutty, savory, and delicious drip coffee.\\n```\\n```menu\\n{\\n\\"title\\": \\"Anjeonki Wheat Waffle\\",\\n\\"rating\\": 3\\n}\\n---\\nI\'m not particularly knowledgeable about desserts, but I still enjoyed it very much.\\n```\\n```menu\\n{\\n\\"title\\": \\"Cake Bar\\",\\n\\"rating\\": 3\\n}\\n---\\nThey offered it complimentary as an apology for the missed order, and it was tasty and enjoyable.\\n```\\n```adcard\\n```\\n## Review\\n\\nI decided to visit this place because it was one of the spots I definitely wanted to check out when looking up places to go in Gongju beforehand.  \\nFortunately, there were plenty of <mark>public parking lots</mark> nearby, so I was able to park easily and comfortably before heading to the cafe.  \\n\\nThe space on the first floor inside the cafe had rather limited seating, but the second floor had plenty of spacious seats that could even accommodate group gatherings, making it great for visits by larger groups.  \\n\\nThe cafe seemed to operate under a concept of researching various types of beans and grains and incorporating them into their menu.  \\nInside the space, there were explanations of different beans, stories about local farmers, and an area where you could purchase related products, which made looking around quite engaging.  \\n\\nHere, you can taste misutgaru (roasted multi-grain shake) made with various types of beans. Wanting to try a bit of everything, I ordered the <mark>Misu Sampler</mark>, the <mark>Signature Drip Coffee</mark>, and the <mark>Anjeonki Wheat Waffle</mark> together.  \\nIn particular, the drip coffee was said to be blended with coffee and grains, which made me very curious about how it would taste.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nAfter ordering, they handed us a cute order number tag with an actual bean placed inside.  \\nWe took our seats and looked around the cafe while waiting for the drinks.  \\n\\nI assumed the drinks would come out quickly after a short wait, but even after waiting for quite a while, nothing arrived—and we even saw guests who arrived after us receiving their drinks first.  \\nThinking something seemed off, I inquired at the counter, and as expected, our order had been missed.  \\nSince the cafe wasn\'t overly crowded, it was a bit disappointing and hard to understand why it was overlooked.  \\n\\nShortly after confirming the oversight, our drinks and desserts were served, and the staff member kindly included a complimentary <mark>Cake Bar</mark> along with an apology.  \\nAlthough it was slightly disappointing initially, in the end, the wait wasn\'t too long, so it was all right.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nThe Misu Sampler came with three varieties of misu: Seonbijabi bean, Cheongtae (green) bean, and Heukgaeng.  \\nTasting each one slowly, I was amazed at how completely different the flavor was depending on the type of bean.  \\nThe flavor closest to the familiar, everyday misutgaru was the Heukgaeng, while the Cheongtae bean and Seonbijabi bean offered deeper, nuttier flavors.  \\nPersonally, my preference in order was Seonbijabi bean, Cheongtae bean, and Heukgaeng.  \\nThe Seonbijabi bean had a sweet and richly rounded flavor, the Cheongtae bean carried a subtle hint of green tea fragrance, and the Heukgaeng was savory yet felt slightly lighter.  \\nIf I visit again next time, I would choose the Seonbijabi bean misu without hesitation.  \\n\\nFor the Signature Drip Coffee, I couldn\'t particularly detect a strong grain presence, but it was still a pleasantly savory and satisfying cup of drip coffee.  \\nWhile it\'s hard for me to give a detailed assessment of desserts like the waffle and cake bar since I don\'t know much about them, they were easy to enjoy and quite tasty.  \\n\\nOverall, the atmosphere was cozy and the beverages were uniquely delicious, making it a great cafe to spend some relaxing time.\\n## Pictures\\n<pictures>\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/2345f9eae1ea25b21988cd31114222eb.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/c859c96486afb81178ea9ecd2005f7cb.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/066b482efc59b1e8167c71d49ad43f20.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/aa886dab2a9ae1b3d9b4b2b1fbdc9b5b.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/dde7e83a83f71764a7877fcae6777dfd.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/797c5ee17b07fa31a480f7224c7a4d48.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/eddfdebb5df37c0dfd4d94949dc53afe.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/bdea8976773c8cc6687f4d4940d6fde6.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/d4c5e7754aa610b5403413bbceb76879.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/3aec4585c12711b2bdbbb81dcede1eed.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/bf6a104f9eb99140e87561fb5998d8ba.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/83a9d71e8549de9a5aab77b291127aaa.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/5754cec8c4d574c9df8e760cb807f599.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/aa2a7b60bae45d60bc8949d6587666fd.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/0170471f7fee54f1dec726488b6f897b.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Gongmuljip\\">\\n</pictures>"}')}}]);